From 3cde49def6e359e994b45eee3f81d1fb37b39ae0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:06:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban placement: a pool worker's built-in
 local-marker hit joins the pool queue

On a gateway whose Board registry entry carries 'linux' and which is not the hub,
a built-in local-marker hit (Keychain, Chrome, a Desktop chat, a ship review's
CI line naming the macOS check, a device skill) no longer keeps the card as a
local row only its creator can claim (workers pick up only runs_on cards).
It queues for the worker_queue label like any portable card, with
capability:tailnet-exec for Mac/Desktop markers and a note naming the route to
the real need. Operator patterns, every other portability reason, an unreadable
registry, the hub (judge path) and the Macs are unchanged.

Observed: t_01a1d2434cf3676c, and t_01a1d2662553185d itself (kept on worker-1
for 'chrome' in its own spec text). Spec: t_01a1d25d4318974b.
---
